			"date": "2023-02-15T01:40:19.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> </p><p>&gt; 1. Does this repeat the same platform defaults mistake that React made?</p><p>What does that mean?</p><p>&gt; 2. Personally, I don’t want to trade away a build step for more client JavaScript.</p><p>CSS and HTML modules don't mean more client-side JS, they mean less of it as you can import CSS and HTML instead of... JS.</p>",
