			"date": "2023-02-15T02:31:51.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://webperf.social/@andydavies\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>andydavies</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> There weren't really rendering concerns, it was just a desire to not have two separate module systems. We can have one module system for an JS, CSS, and HTML, we just have to finish ...</p>",
